      "model_authored_rationale": "Iterated local search (2-opt + Or-opt with neighbour lists and don't-look bits)\nfor Euclidean TSP, replacing the reference's best-improvement 2-opt restarts.\n\nRationale (exploratory but standard practice): the common reference runs 24\nnearest-neighbour starts, each refined by at most 300 best-improvement 2-opt\nmoves.  Such tours are plain 2-opt local optima, typically several percent above\noptimal for n=320.  This method keeps the same feature-only prediction contract\nbut spends the generous per-instance time budget on a much stronger search:\n\n  * full distance matrix + K=10 nearest-neighbour candidate lists,\n  * first-improvement 2-opt *and* Or-opt (segments of length 1..3, both\n    orientations, both insertion sides) driven by a don't-look-bit queue,\n  * iterated local search: double-bridge kicks, re-optimising only the eight\n    touched endpoints, accepting strict improvements, keeping the best tour.\n\nChunked calls into numba let Python enforce a wall-clock budget per instance\n(total budget shared equally over the split), so the whole split finishes inside\nthe execution limit regardless of split size.  No labels are used; each instance\nis solved independently from its coordinates only.\n\nLimitation: improvement over the reference is measured here only on training\ninstances during train (held-out development/audit scores are not visible), and\nsolution quality depends on the realised per-instance time slice.",
      "selected_findings": {
        "method": "ILS(2-opt+Or-opt, neighbour lists, don't-look bits)",
        "candidates_K": 10,
