      "model_authored_rationale": "TREC coarse question type: reference-style SVM plus question-structure and lexicon features.\n\nRationale (exploratory, not yet verified): the parent b1-s0 stacked three blocks and got\n0.1194 development error against the reference's 0.1340. The blocks were word 1-3grams,\nchar_wb 2-5grams, and positional wh/head-word features. It did not qualify at\nconfirmation, so its true gain is probably below the 10% target. The error is likely to\nbe driven by rare head words (\"what [rare noun] ...\") and definitional DESC questions.\n\nThis step adds a fourth, independently weighted block of hand-written features:\n- a small semantic lexicon mapping head nouns and adjectives to coarse classes, for\n  example city->LOC, author->HUM, year/long->NUM, color->ENTY, mean/why->DESC and\n  stand/acronym->ABBR;\n- short \"what is X\" definitional patterns;\n- \"stand for\" and \"mean\" cues;\n- capitalisation and all-caps (acronym) cues.\n\nSetting the lexicon weight to 0 reproduces the parent configuration, so the parent is\nscored inside the same grid. Block weights and C are chosen by GroupKFold CV on\napi.train_groups.\n\nTo reduce selection noise, the final model averages SVM decision functions over the\ntop-k CV configurations. k is chosen from out-of-fold decisions. The model object holds\nonly standard sklearn objects and numbers; feature text is rebuilt by module code in\npredict.",
